BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nolta-2026-deadline-full-paper@scientific-conference-calendar
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260520
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260521
SUMMARY:[Nonlinear Dynamics & Chaos][Complex Systems & Network Science] NOL
 TA 2026 - Regular and special-session papers (cutoff time unannounced)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Symposium on Nonlinear Theory a
 nd Its Applications\nWebsite: https://nolta2026.org/\nSource URL: https:/
 /nolta2026.org/\nLocation: Grenoble\, France\nTopics: Nonlinear Dynamics 
 & Chaos\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Deep Representation Learnin
 g\, Control & Robotics\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based\nConfidence
 : confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-06\nNotes: Annual IEICE NOLTA sym
 posium\; official final extensions supersede older April/July dates. Proc
 eedings papers\, with neural networks and deep AI explicitly in scope. De
 adline hours use estimated end-of-day AoE. Size is an editorial category.
 \nScope: Nonlinear theory and its applications\, centered on chaos\, bifu
 rcations\, oscillations\, synchronization\, nonlinear circuits\, and comp
 lex networks. Neural computation\, evolutionary algorithms\, control\, an
 d signal processing connect to this nonlinear-systems focus. Individual a
 pplication examples are not taken as additional specialist identities.\nA
 dditional topics: Signal Processing\, Evolutionary Computation & Optimiza
 tion\nScope sources (2026): https://nolta2026.org/\nScope last checked: 2
 026-10-07\nOfficial deadline day\; exact cutoff hour/timezone is unannoun
 ced. Verify the organizer's submission portal.
URL:https://nolta2026.org/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:log-2026-deadline-abstract@scientific-conference-calendar
DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20260806T115900Z
DTEND:20260806T125900Z
SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Deep Representation Learning] LoG 2026 - Abstrac
 t registration deadline (both tracks)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Learning on Graphs Conference\nWebsite: https
 ://logconference.org/\nSource URL: https://logconference.org/cfp/\nLocati
 on: Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA\nTopics: Machine Learning\, Deep Represe
 ntation Learning\, Complex Systems & Network Science\, Learning Theory & 
 Statistical Foundations\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / non-arch
 ival extended abstracts\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-1
 0-07\nNotes: Fifth annual edition\, in person at Northeastern University.
  Extended Aug 5/7 deadlines replace the struck-through July 29/Aug 1 date
 s. Proceedings papers and non-archival extended abstracts share the regis
 tration and final submission cutoffs\, represented as one route. The TMLR
  presentation track requires an already published paper\, so it is not a 
 new-paper opportunity. LoG is distinct from LOD/AIS. Size M is an editori
 al estimate.\nScope: Learning on graphs and geometry: graph neural networ
 ks\, equivariant models\, graph kernels\, geometric and graph generative 
 models\, and statistical theory for structured data. Graph signal process
 ing\, causal graph models\, robustness\, and scalable graph-learning infr
 astructure are meaningful extensions. A graph or geometric contribution s
 hould remain central\, even in an application such as language or molecul
 ar modeling.\nAdditional topics: Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\
 , Signal Processing\, Robustness & Safety\, ML Systems & Infrastructure\n
 Scope sources (2026): https://logconference.org/cfp/\nScope last checked:
  2026-10-07
URL:https://logconference.org/cfp/
END:VEVENT
